        "answer_id": "ans_36ee1e8ff52740ebb8b3a9422c25ec0c",
        "locale": "en",
        "depth": "beginner",
        "status": "answered",
        "uncertainty": "partial",
        "reason": "supported_explanation",
        "answer_text": "Fuzhou shadow puppetry is listed as traditional theatre from Wafangdian, Liaoning.\n\nTo go a little deeper: shadow puppetry works because light travels in straight lines. A flat figure held close to the screen casts a small, sharp shadow, while moving it farther back makes the shadow grow and blur. Puppeteers use this trick to make characters seem to leap, shrink or loom large — a bit like holding your hand near a lamp versus across the room. What do you think a bigger shadow would make an audience feel?",
